      "description": "The (Vowel + Consonant)உயிர்மெய் எழுத்துக்கள் are compound letters in Tamil formed by combining a consonant (மெய்) with a vowel (உயிர்). For example, the consonant ழ்(Zh) combines with vowels to form ழ, ழா, ழி, ழீ, ழு, ழூ, ழெ, ழே, ழை, ழொ, ழோ, and ழௌ."
